# catalog/lib/build-agents.env
#
# Maps the finite `build.agent` enum in schemas/cicd.schema.json to real build-agent
# image references. This is the single place that mapping lives - Tasks resolve it via
# `resolve-build-agent-image.yaml`, they never hardcode an image per agent name.
# Keep this file's keys in sync with the `build.agent` enum in the schema.
#
# These point at real, existing upstream images (Docker Hub official images), NOT
# custom platform-curated ones - an earlier version of this file pointed at
# ghcr.io/platform-cicd/build-agents/* images that sounded like they'd been built and
# published somewhere, but never actually were. Caught live, as ImagePullBackOff on the
# first real pipeline run, not in review. Building and hardening dedicated
# platform-owned build-agent images (pinned patch versions, pre-warmed caches, non-root
# by default) is a reasonable Phase 2+ enhancement, but this file should never claim
# that's already done when it isn't - point at something real until it's real.
#
# Deliberately NOT the -alpine variants: every catalog step script is bash
# (#!/usr/bin/env bash), and Alpine images don't ship bash by default (busybox sh
# only) - run-tests.yaml/run-integration-tests.yaml/build-image.yaml's run-build-script
# all execute inside whatever image this file resolves to. Caught live as step exit code
# 127 ("command not found") on the first real pipeline run, not in review - verified
# bash actually exists in each image below before switching, not assumed.
nodejs-18=docker.io/library/node:18
nodejs-20=docker.io/library/node:20
nodejs-22=docker.io/library/node:22
openjdk-17=docker.io/library/eclipse-temurin:17-jdk
openjdk-21=docker.io/library/eclipse-temurin:21-jdk
python-3.11=docker.io/library/python:3.11
go-1.22=docker.io/library/golang:1.22
